  "notes": "Cash basis village. Governmental lines from the 2023 Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5); fund balances 675,200 -> 761,864 roll forward (p5). Cash: Cash and cash equivalents plus restricted cash from the governmental funds statement (p3; 2022 comparative column for beginning); fund balance also includes due from other funds 285,445 and due from other governments 10,902. Business-type from the cash-basis proprietary statement (p7; total ties to the Statement of Activities business-type expenses 278,848 and revenues p2); capital outlay 88,469 is printed among nonoperating items and recorded as a disbursement; proceeds from sale of asset 302 is business_type other_financing. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1), Governmental and Business-type columns (as FY2024; kept because it carries internal balances); totals from the 2023 Total column. Business-type measure cash (cash-basis proprietary statement, as FY2024). Detail: General Fund revenues and other financing from its budget schedule (p8); General Fund expenditures from the departmental combining schedule (p15, more detailed; the p8 object lines 115,457/72,354/5,031/76,520/75,623 are its Total column, not recorded twice; budget_final not available by department). Street, Debt Service, Keno, Water, Sewer, Trash budget schedules p9-14. Zero-actual lines with only a budget (General transfers out (100,000); Street capital outlay 230,000 and transfers in 100,000; Water debt service 500,000) not recorded. Trash schedule prints no total revenues line (single line 101,724). Read pages 1-15 of 15"
